{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MRwLoiFnqfHW1BLBGa6arw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Product document for `fix-loop-own-words`.\n2\t#\n3\t# Its concepts cover every step of E2E-001, and the glossary defines\n4\t# every term they declare but \"latency\"; the fix adds the entry that\n5\t# defines it, its meaning as the person put it in their own words.\n6\t\n7\ttitle: \"Fixture host project\"\n8\t\n9\tdescription:\n10\t  summary: >-\n11\t    A single MCP service, used by the true-bdd fixtures as the host\n12\t    project a scenario registry describes.\n13\t\n14\troles:\n15\t  - name: Operator\n16\t    definition: Runs the MCP service and watches what it answers.\n17\t  - name: Client Developer\n18\t    definition: Writes the clients that send the MCP service its requests.\n19\t\n20\tglossary:\n21\t  - term: mcp service\n22\t    means: >-\n23\t      The service this project builds: it takes a message from a client\n24\t      and answers it. What every Scenario of the project observes.\n25\t  - term: reply\n26\t    means: >-\n27\t      What the MCP service sends back for one message, and how long it\n28\t      took to arrive. A client waits on it, so its content and its delay\n29\t      are both behaviour.\n30\t\n31\tconcepts:\n32\t  given:\n33\t    - concept: service running\n34\t      means: The MCP service has started and accepts requests.\n35\t      terms: [mcp service]\n36\t  when:\n37\t    - concept: message sent\n38\t      means: A role sends a stated message to the MCP service, once.\n39\t      terms: [mcp service]\n40\t  then:\n41\t    - concept: answer\n42\t      means: The MCP service's reply to the message is exactly a stated text.\n43\t      terms: [mcp service, reply]\n44\t    - concept: reply time\n45\t      means: The latency of the MCP service's reply to the message is at most a stated number of milliseconds.\n46\t      terms: [mcp service, reply, latency]\n47\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id